## Topology chooses the target

The finite tropical projective line is normalized by $x=x_1-x_0$ and is represented by $\mathbb{R}$. The endpoint-completed version is compact. Since compactness is preserved by homeomorphism and $\mathbb{R}$ is noncompact, the compactified source cannot be homeomorphic to the ordinary real line.

